              <section id="section-1" class="terms-section" aria-labelledby="section-1-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">1</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Overview</p>
                    <h2 id="section-1-title" class="section-title">Introduction &amp; Acceptance of Terms</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>Welcome to ZenoPay. These Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of ZenoPay’s websites, hosted payment pages, merchant tools, APIs, mobile experiences, dashboards, settlement features, and any related services that we make available from time to time (collectively, the “Services”). By accessing, browsing, registering for, integrating with, or using any part of the Services, you agree to be bound by these Terms.</p>
                  <p>ZenoPay operates as a modern fintech platform that helps individuals, merchants, and business partners move money, collect payments, manage balances, and monitor transactions. Because our Services are connected to regulated financial flows, your use of the Services is subject to operational, security, risk, and compliance requirements that are essential to protecting users and the broader payment ecosystem.</p>

                  <div class="callout-box info-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-circle-info callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Important Notice</strong>
                      Review these Terms carefully before creating an account or processing transactions through ZenoPay. If you do not agree to these Terms, you must not use the Services.
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Binding Agreement</h3>
                  <p>These Terms form a binding legal agreement between you and ZenoPay. If you are accessing or using the Services on behalf of a company, institution, or other legal entity, you represent and warrant that you are authorized to bind that entity to these Terms, and references to “you” will include that entity.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Supplemental Policies</h3>
                  <p>Your use of specific features may also be governed by product guidelines, implementation documentation, privacy notices, fee schedules, acceptable use rules, and security requirements published by ZenoPay. Where applicable, those supplemental materials are incorporated into these Terms by reference.</p>
                </div>
              </section>

              <section id="section-2" class="terms-section" aria-labelledby="section-2-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">2</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Key Terms</p>
                    <h2 id="section-2-title" class="section-title">Definitions</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>For clarity and consistency throughout these Terms, the following definitions apply:</p>

                  <dl class="definition-list">
                    <div class="definition-item">
                      <dt>Account</dt>
                      <dd>The ZenoPay profile, dashboard access, and associated credentials used to access and manage the Services.</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="definition-item">
                      <dt>Merchant</dt>
                      <dd>Any business, sole proprietor, nonprofit, or other organization using ZenoPay to accept, route, reconcile, or settle payments.</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="definition-item">
                      <dt>Customer</dt>
                      <dd>An end user, payer, buyer, subscriber, or recipient who interacts with a Merchant or directly uses ZenoPay features.</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="definition-item">
                      <dt>Payment Method</dt>
                      <dd>Any supported card, bank account, wallet, transfer rail, local method, tokenized credential, or alternative payment instrument connected to the Services.</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="definition-item">
                      <dt>Transaction</dt>
                      <dd>Any payment authorization, capture, payout, transfer, refund, reversal, chargeback, adjustment, or settlement event processed through ZenoPay.</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="definition-item">
                      <dt>Content</dt>
                      <dd>Any text, data, software, designs, documentation, trademarks, layouts, graphics, or other material made available through the Services.</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="definition-item">
                      <dt>Applicable Law</dt>
                      <dd>All local, national, international, regulatory, sanctions, anti-money laundering, privacy, consumer, and financial-services rules that apply to your use of the Services.</dd>
                    </div>
                  </dl>
                </div>
              </section>

              <section id="section-3" class="terms-section" aria-labelledby="section-3-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">3</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Who May Use ZenoPay</p>
                    <h2 id="section-3-title" class="section-title">User Eligibility</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>To use the Services, you must meet our eligibility requirements at all times. Eligibility may vary by feature, geography, payment method, and risk profile.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Minimum Age and Legal Capacity</h3>
                  <p>You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of majority in your jurisdiction, and have the legal authority to enter into binding contracts. If you access the Services on behalf of a business, you must be duly authorized to act for that business.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Supported Jurisdictions</h3>
                  <p>ZenoPay may only be available in selected countries or regions. Access to the Services may be restricted, limited, or suspended where regulatory approval is unavailable or where service delivery would create unacceptable legal or operational risk.</p>

                  <div class="callout-box warning-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Restricted Use</strong>
                      You may not use ZenoPay if you are located in, ordinarily resident in, or operating from a sanctioned or prohibited jurisdiction, or if you are included on any relevant watchlist or denied-party list.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <section id="section-4" class="terms-section" aria-labelledby="section-4-title">
