                    <h2 id="section-5-title" class="section-title">User Responsibilities</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>You are responsible for using the Services lawfully, ethically, and in accordance with industry best practices. This includes maintaining internal controls appropriate for your transaction volume and business model.</p>

                  <ul>
                    <li>Use the Services only for authorized and legitimate business or personal purposes.</li>
                    <li>Ensure that any data submitted to ZenoPay is accurate, lawful, and properly consented.</li>
                    <li>Review transaction activity and reconcile balances regularly.</li>
                    <li>Maintain sufficient fraud, chargeback, and customer support controls.</li>
                    <li>Cooperate with operational, security, and regulatory inquiries.</li>
                  </ul>

                  <div class="callout-box info-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-shield-halved callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Operational Best Practice</strong>
                      Merchants should maintain a clear refund policy, visible business descriptors, timely customer support channels, and documented escalation workflows to reduce disputes and customer harm.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <section id="section-6" class="terms-section" aria-labelledby="section-6-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">6</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Transaction Flow</p>
                    <h2 id="section-6-title" class="section-title">Payment Terms</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>ZenoPay provides infrastructure that enables payment initiation, authorization, capture, transfer, settlement, reconciliation, and payout workflows. The timing and availability of these processes may vary depending on risk, banking partners, and payment rails.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Processing and Settlement</h3>
                  <p>Authorizations, captures, and settlements are subject to network rules, banking cut-off times, fraud controls, holds, and reconciliation procedures. Settlement timing displayed in your dashboard is an estimate and may change based on operational review.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Refunds, Reversals, and Holds</h3>
                  <p>ZenoPay may process refunds, reversals, reserves, or temporary holds where required to manage risk, comply with law, support investigations, or resolve disputes. Funds may be delayed while suspicious or incomplete activity is reviewed.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Third-Party Dependencies</h3>
                  <p>Certain outcomes depend on banks, card networks, local schemes, and external service providers. ZenoPay is not responsible for delays caused solely by third-party infrastructure outside our reasonable control.</p>
                </div>
              </section>

              <section id="section-7" class="terms-section" aria-labelledby="section-7-title">
