                  <span class="section-number">11</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Risk Allocation</p>
                    <h2 id="section-11-title" class="section-title">Limitation of Liability</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>To the maximum extent permitted by Applicable Law, ZenoPay is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, lost data, lost revenue, or business interruption arising out of or related to the Services.</p>
                  <p>Where liability cannot lawfully be excluded, ZenoPay’s aggregate liability will be limited to the amounts paid by you to ZenoPay for the affected Services in the three months preceding the event giving rise to the claim, or the minimum amount required by law, whichever is greater.</p>

                  <div class="callout-box info-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-scale-balanced callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Scope of Limitation</strong>
                      These limitations apply regardless of the theory of liability and even if a limited remedy fails of its essential purpose, except where exclusions are not permitted by law.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <section id="section-12" class="terms-section" aria-labelledby="section-12-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">12</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Resolving Issues</p>
                    <h2 id="section-12-title" class="section-title">Dispute Resolution</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>If a dispute arises, the parties agree to make reasonable efforts to resolve it informally before initiating formal proceedings. Prompt notice and supporting information should be provided to enable efficient investigation.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Informal Resolution</h3>
                  <p>You should first contact ZenoPay support or legal operations with a detailed description of the issue, affected transactions, and the relief requested. Many issues can be resolved through reconciliation, clarification, or operational review.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Formal Proceedings</h3>
                  <p>If a dispute cannot be resolved informally, it may be submitted to the competent courts or dispute forums specified by applicable contract or law. Nothing in this section prevents either party from seeking interim injunctive relief where necessary to protect rights or prevent imminent harm.</p>
                </div>
              </section>

              <section id="section-13" class="terms-section" aria-labelledby="section-13-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">13</span>
                  <div>
